Side finding from the #66 sondierung (verified live 2026-08-17 by langertha-llm-advisor).

AKI.IO ships an Anthropic-compatible interface next to its native API and its OpenAI-compatible
one (which Langertha covers as Engine::AKIOpenAI):

  base URL:  https://aki.io/anthropic
  endpoint:  /v1/messages
  auth:      x-api-key: <AKI key>   (anthropic-version accepted but not required)
  streaming: SSE
  models:    /anthropic/v1/models

That is a FIFTH consumer of the existing Role::AnthropicCompatible (after Anthropic,
MiniMaxAnthropic, MoonshotAnthropic, LMStudioAnthropic) and it is EU/GDPR-hosted — the same
selling point as the existing AKI engines.

Implementation would be the usual thin shim: `extends Langertha::Engine::AnthropicBase`, url
default + _build_api_key (LANGERTHA_AKI_API_KEY, same env as Engine::AKI) + default_model.

Quirk to encode/document: unknown model IDs do NOT error — the endpoint silently falls back to
MiniMax M2.5. Worth a POD warning at minimum.

Nice side effect: this is direct evidence that ADR 0013 (envelope as composed role) paid off on
the Anthropic side, while #66 concludes the opposite for the single-consumer dialects.
Built. Every wire fact was confirmed from AKI.IO public documentation only — no live call was made against the endpoint (maintainer constraint).

Confirmed from https://aki.io/docs/compatibility/anthropic-api-compatibility/ and https://aki.io/docs/compatibility/for-ai-coding-agents/:
- base URL https://aki.io/anthropic, endpoint /v1/messages ("AKI.IO API internally appends /v1/messages")
- auth x-api-key, raw value, docs say explicitly "NO Bearer prefix"
- anthropic-version accepted but not required
- SSE streaming via stream, system as top-level parameter, default_max_output_tokens 8192
- 9 model ids, and verbatim: "Requests to unknown model names will fall back onto the Minimax M2.5 model."

NOT confirmed: tool calling on /anthropic (docs list no tools parameter for this endpoint; tool calling is documented only for /openai/v1). The engine inherits the anthropic tool wire format from AnthropicBase and the POD says plainly that it is unverified. See #102. Model discovery is also contradictory in AKI docs (/anthropic/v1/models vs /openai/v1/models), so the engine uses Role::StaticModels like the MiniMax/Moonshot shims instead of relying on either.

Files: lib/Langertha/Engine/AKIAnthropic.pm (new), t/26_akianthropic_requests.t (new), t/10_engine_hierarchy.t, lib/Langertha/Engine/AnthropicBase.pm (extender POD list). Suite green recursively, perlcritic clean. Not committed. Follow-ups in #103.
